        <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 20px;">* Valid for max. inrush of 50 x I_L</p>

        <h4 style="font-size: 16px; margin-top: 30px;">Example for lamp load calculation:</h4>
        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Due to many varieties of lamps and ballasts we advice to take the current load as base for reference. The lamp table considers already the inrush peaks and other lamp parameters. The formula I_P/U can be used for calculation if only the voltage and power is known.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Fluorescent lamp with conventional ballast, uncompensated, the lamp operating current I = 1.5 A, voltage U = 230 V. <br> 1 pole of ESB24 can be loaded with max. 22 A, see lamp table => 22A/1.5A = 14.66 => 14 lamps <br> 1 pole of ESB20 can be loaded with max. 9 A, see lamp table => 9A/1.5A = 6 => 6 lamps</p>
        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Please use the referring value in the table stated above and divide it with the current stated on the lamp. This will lead into the number of lamps which can be switched.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 14px;">E.g.: ESB24 used for LED lamps: 7 A ( = 7000 mA) / 85 mA = 82.23 => 82 lamps</p>
    </div>

